ct","relevance":"primary","title":"Mutations in the Neuroblastoma Amplified Sequence gene in a family affected by Acrofrontofacionasal Dysostosis type 1."},{"id":"paper:22052670","type":"Paper","label":"Prontera et al. (2011)","pmid":"22052670","year":2011,"content_level":"title","relevance":"background","title":"Acrofrontofacionasal dysostosis 1 in two sisters of Indian origin."},{"id":"finding:22052670:1","type":"Finding","label":"Prontera et al. (2011) reported acrofrontofacionasal dysostosis type 1 in 2 sisters of Indian origin.","pmid":"22052670","section":"clinical_features"},{"id":"finding:29929043:1","type":"Finding","label":"Palagano et al. (2018) studied an Indian family with 2 affected sibs diagnosed with acrofrontofacionasal dysostosis type 1. They described it as an extremely rare autosomal recessive syndrome with facial and skeletal abnormalities, short stature, and intellectual disability.","pmid":"29929043","section":"clinical_features"},{"id":"gene:NBAS","type":"Gene","label":"NBAS"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0000271","type":"Phenotype","label":"Abnormality of the face","hpo_id":"HP:0000271"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0000924","type":"Phenotype","label":"Abnormality of the skeletal system","hpo_id":"HP:0000924"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0004322","type":"Phenotype","label":"Short stature","hpo_id":"HP:0004322"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0001249","type":"Phenotype","label":"Intellectual disability","hpo_id":"HP:0001249"},{"id":"inh:AR","type":"Inheritance","label":"Autosomal recessive","hpo_id":"HP:0000007"},{"id":"finding:29929043:2","type":"Finding","label":"In 2 affected sibs from an Indian family with acrofrontofacionasal dysostosis, Palagano et al. (2018) used exome sequencing to identify a novel homozygous truncating mutation in the NBAS gene. Overexpressing the truncated NBAS protein in HEK293T cells impaired both nonsense-mediated decay and Golgi-to-endoplasmic reticulum retrograde traffic.","pmid":"29929043","section":"molecular_genetics"},{"id":"variant:NBAS:raw:novel homozygous truncati